<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97497" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύγγᾰμ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>united in wedlock,
			married</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλῳ</span> to another,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				212
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. δάμαρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					1220
				</span></i>
			: as Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύγγαμος, ὁ</span> or ἡ, <i>husband</i> or <i>wife</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>A.</u>
				595
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(3).1188
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Melos</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally, <i>connected by marriage</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				[428]
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύγγαμός σοι Ζεύς</span>
			<i>sharing</i> your <i>marriage-bed</i>, of Amphitryon, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HF</u>
				149
			</span></i>: in pl., <i>the rival wives of one man</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				182
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
